{# The brand lockup — the app's masthead, in email-safe form (operator 2026-10-05): the waveform
   mark, then the tagline above the wordmark, in the app's default palette (brand #efa843, muted
   #acb2c2, cream #f0eae0). ONE partial for every email, so the branding cannot drift per template.

   The mark is a PNG, not the SVG the app uses: Gmail and Outlook do not render SVG. It is served
   by the player (`/brand/email-mark.png`, 3x for retina) from the tenant's own origin; a static
   .png passes the pre-launch gate. `alt=""` because the wordmark beside it is REAL TEXT — a client
   that blocks images still shows "Close Listening", which an image-only logo would lose. #}
<table role="presentation" cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" border="0" style="margin:0 0 18px;">
  <tr>
    <td valign="middle" style="padding:0 10px 0 0;"><img src="{{ app_origin }}/brand/email-mark.png" width="28" height="30" alt="" style="display:block;border:0;outline:none;text-decoration:none;"></td>
    <td valign="middle">
      <div style="font-size:10px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.16em;text-transform:uppercase;color:#acb2c2;line-height:1.3;">Listen. Understand. Remember.</div>
      <div style="font-size:21px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:-.01em;color:#f0eae0;line-height:1.2;">Close Listening</div>
    </td>
  </tr>
</table>
